WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.427
- I think the homeless in general

00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:06.257
just feel that they've
been completely forgotten

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:09.537
by society, that nobody cares about them.

00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:12.907
Nobody cares if they wake up tomorrow.

00:00:12.907 --> 00:00:14.784
They might even feel like they

00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:17.789
think that people hope that
they don't wake up tomorrow.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:19.777
And I didn't think that
anybody should have

00:00:19.777 --> 00:00:21.673
to feel like that, so I decided

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:24.305
that when I became a PA, that I wanted

00:00:24.305 --> 00:00:27.273
to focus on the homeless population.

00:00:27.273 --> 00:00:30.606
(gentle, hopeful music)

00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:36.031
(car door shutting)

00:00:36.031 --> 00:00:37.812
(car starting)

00:00:37.812 --> 00:00:41.670
So Street Medicine is
really a program that was born

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.436
out of the idea that everybody matters.

00:00:44.436 --> 00:00:47.419
We see that there's certain
segments of the population that

00:00:47.419 --> 00:00:50.099
just don't access healthcare
the way everybody else does.

00:00:50.099 --> 00:00:52.013
(traffic speeding by)

00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:55.013
(church bell rings)

00:00:56.029 --> 00:00:59.046
(church bell rings)

00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:02.266
Because Allentown is a
relatively small city,

00:01:02.266 --> 00:01:04.185
it is still surrounded by woods so,

00:01:04.185 --> 00:01:06.429
most of the homeless you're not gonna see

00:01:06.429 --> 00:01:08.358
sleeping outside on the street

00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:10.309
so they go live in the woods in tents,

00:01:10.309 --> 00:01:14.925
so that's usually where we have
to go to find our patients.

00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:18.240
I have a backpack with
over 20 medications.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.992
We have a EKG machine.

00:01:19.992 --> 00:01:21.628
We do point-of-care testing

00:01:21.628 --> 00:01:23.295
where we can get different blood work.

00:01:23.295 --> 00:01:26.587
The whole idea is to
deliver quality care on-site

00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:29.359
in a place where the
patient feels comfortable.

00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:32.442
(train horn honking)

00:01:34.134 --> 00:01:36.013
(train horn honking)

00:01:36.013 --> 00:01:37.493
(birds tweeting)

00:01:37.493 --> 00:01:39.061
Do you still have that inhaler, Mike?

00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:39.894
- [Mike] Yeah.

00:01:39.894 --> 00:01:41.428
- How often are you using it?

00:01:41.428 --> 00:01:43.595
- [Voiceover] 102 over 68.

00:01:44.512 --> 00:01:46.648
- Everything we do is completely free.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:49.812
We provide free medications, free labs,

00:01:49.812 --> 00:01:53.318
free diagnostic studies, so
they don't need insurance,

00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:56.116
and we have the same incredible people

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.704
that see them all the time.

00:01:57.704 --> 00:01:59.558
They get to know us and trust us,

00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:03.509
and we're lucky enough that
they allow us to help them.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:06.187
Okay, just breathe normal.

00:02:06.187 --> 00:02:09.896
Doing this job can be extremely difficult.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.803
You just see things that are really hard

00:02:12.803 --> 00:02:16.132
to see and sometimes feel helpless,

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:18.131
but one of the things that I always try

00:02:18.131 --> 00:02:21.939
to do is just try and
completely forget myself in it,

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:23.999
to remember that this
is not about me at all.

00:02:23.999 --> 00:02:25.900
It's just about the patients.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.355
It doesn't matter if I'm tired.

00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:29.184
It doesn't matter if I'm frustrated

00:02:29.184 --> 00:02:31.223
with trying to help somebody.

00:02:31.223 --> 00:02:32.887
It just doesn't matter about me.

00:02:32.887 --> 00:02:34.921
It matters about them.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:39.025
So I try and focus on
them and their needs.

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:43.192
(dry leaves and sticks
crunching under feet)

